  "body": "P0 (#96): verify's rapid law skipped every vertical rapid as \"a retract through the tool's own kerf\" - including rapids going DOWN into uncut stock - so any op's vertical rapid into declared stock posted silently.\n\n**What changed**\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/rapids.rs`: a downward vertical rapid that ends below the stock surface left by earlier cuts, inside the stock, is `RapidInStock`; peck re-entries down their own earlier plunge and retracts up stay clean.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/turning_rapids.rs` (one call in `generate.rs`): drops `RapidInStock` only for turning ops' rapids along the spindle axis (no XY travel) - on a lathe world Z is the spindle, and a column reading cannot see what the part or earlier passes removed beside the bar (false conviction). Those rapids were never checked before this PR either; checking them properly in the meridian plane is #103. Every non-turning op, and turning sideways rapids, keep every conviction.\n\n**Triage of every newly failing test** (all 193 debug binaries of app/ui/motion/sim run)\n\n| Test(s) | Op | Rapid | Stock top | Verdict | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| posting: 6 on `contour_and_drill` | Contour, top 5, clearance 10, retract 8 | move 1, Z10 -> Z7 beside the 5 mm box | 10 | real collision | stock 10 -> 5 mm (and the Deep1 shank fixture) |\n| control_comp: 3 | same contour | move 1 | 10 | real collision | stock 10 -> 5 mm |\n| operations: `the_shell_switch_sends_the_pocket_to_the_offset_engine` | Pocket3D, top 5 | move 1 | 20 | real collision | stock 20 -> 5 mm |\n| motion pocket3d_hsm: 2 | Pocket3D, top -5 | move 1 | 0 (test's verify setup) | real by the fixture | verify stock top 0 -> -5 |\n| turning_bore: 3 | Boring | move 0, along the axis | 110 mm box | false conviction | `turning_rapids` |\n| turning_contour: 5 | Taper / Chamfer / Multi-pass | move 0, along the axis | box over the bar | false conviction | `turning_rapids` |\n| lathe_post: `profile_rough_and_finish_post_to_the_lathe_golden` | Profile rough+finish | move 0 | 40 mm box | false conviction | `turning_rapids` |\n\nGoldens unchanged (`contour_control_comp.nc`, `fanuc-lathe/profile_rough_finish.nc` byte for byte).\n\n**Pinned by** `vertical_rapids` (sim, 4) and `vertical_rapid_stock` (app, 2: a contour under a 10 mm block is named at generation and refused at the post; posts clean over stock to its top).\n\n**Gates**: all 193 debug binaries run once; the failing ones + 117 binaries incl. all 16 ui suites re-run green on the final build; clippy -D warnings clean. Not re-run on the final build: lathe_field_sim, center_cut_multiaxis (slow lane), motion and sim binaries (green earlier with the same law; the app change only removes turning warnings).\n\n**Follow-ups**: #103 (turning axial rapids checked in the meridian plane), #104 (named warning when an op's top is below the stock top).\n\nChangelog: fix(sim,app): a vertical rapid going down into uncut stock is now a rapid-in-stock conviction and blocks the post (turned ops' rapids along the spindle axis keep their old reading)\n\nFixes #96\n",
